    "text": "Tech Stocks\nMicron’s stock rebounds after ‘healthy’ reset, and analysts see blue skies ahead\nMicron shares trade cheaply relative to S&P 500 peers, but two analysts point to ways the valuation multiple can expand\nMemory stocks are back on the upswing, and Morgan Stanley analysts say their recent breather was necessary to support more explosive gains.\nWhile Micron’s stock rose 11.7% on Thursday, it’s off nearly 10% from its peak close on June 3. Shares of South Korea-listed memory-chip makers Samsung Electronics KR:005930 and SK Hynix KR:000660 are down 18% and 13%, respectively, from their recent closing highs.",
